# SRNN Model Parity

This note records the flat model architecture boundary before hierarchical
modeling starts.

## Source References

- Paper: `docs/social-attention.pdf`
- Upstream reference: `socialAttention/social-attention/srnn-pytorch/srnn/model.py`
- Current model: `src/models/flat.py`

## Architecture Components

The current flat model uses the same component split as the upstream
social-attention SRNN:

- `NodeRNN`: embeds node coordinates, combines temporal and spatial edge context,
  then advances a node LSTM.
- `EdgeRNN`: embeds edge coordinate deltas and advances an edge LSTM.
- `temporal_edge_rnn`: processes self-edges across adjacent frames.
- `spatial_edge_rnn`: processes inter-node spatial edges within each frame.
- `EdgeAttention`: attends from each node's temporal edge state over its spatial
  edge states.

## MABe Adaptation Boundary

The implementation keeps the training-facing output contract:

```text
[time, nodes, 5]
```

where `5` is the bivariate Gaussian parameter vector per node.

The graph is still the MABe keypoint graph from `src/st_graph.py`, so this is an
architecture parity implementation adapted to the current graph contract rather
than a byte-for-byte port of the upstream pedestrian code.

## Verify

```sh
python -m pytest tests/test_models_flat.py -q
```
